# VTID-03992 — commands run, verbatim intent

## 1. Background audit (Explore agent, read-only, no code changed)

Dispatched to check whether the class of leak VTID-03990 fixed exists on
other real-member-facing surfaces. Findings (ranked by risk):
- HIGH: GET /api/v1/community/members (community-members.ts / -repository.ts)
  — no bot/test exclusion, default sort "newest" by registration_seq.
- HIGH: ORB voice superlatives.ts / community-member-ranker.ts — same gap,
  shared getHiddenUserIds()/fetchVisibleProfileUserIds() exclusion logic.
- MEDIUM/HIGH (unconfirmed): matchmaking match_targets candidate pool.
- MEDIUM: connect-people-repository.ts fetchPrimaryTenantUsers() iterates
  all primary-tenant users; VITANA_BOT_USER_ID declared in connect-people.ts
  but never referenced (dead code).
- LOW: admin-facing "all users" lists (not fixed here, admins already know).

## 2. Empirical confirmation (read-only against production)

select p.user_id, p.display_name, p.registration_seq, p.created_at,
       exists(select 1 from global_community_profiles gcp where gcp.user_id = p.user_id and gcp.is_visible = false) as hidden
from profiles p
where p.user_id in ('887b34cb-9ee9-47dc-ad53-db5be1869846','856c30ed-7136-4bc5-8bfe-86a1e8ea1401');
-- => claude-code-agent: registration_seq=246, hidden=false
--    operator-autopilot: registration_seq=247, hidden=false

select max(registration_seq) as max_seq, count(*) as total_profiles from profiles;
-- => max_seq=247 (== operator-autopilot's own row), total_profiles=225
-- CONFIRMED: both bot accounts are the #1 and #2 results of the
-- Members Directory's default "newest" sort, right now, in production.
-- (full output saved to outputs/members-directory-exposure.json)

## 3. Matchmaking investigation (read-only against production)

select to_regclass('public.match_targets') as match_targets_exists,
       to_regclass('public.matches_daily') as matches_daily_exists,
       to_regclass('public.daily_matches') as daily_matches_exists;
-- => match_targets_exists=null, matches_daily_exists=null, daily_matches_exists='daily_matches'
-- CONFIRMED: match_targets/matches_daily (the candidate-pool schema the
-- audit flagged) do not exist live — dead, never-deployed migration.

select column_name from information_schema.columns where table_schema='public' and table_name='daily_matches' order by ordinal_position;
-- => id, user_id, matched_user_id, match_score, match_reasons, created_at, expires_at, viewed_at, action

select count(*) as total_rows,
  count(*) filter (where user_id in ('887b34cb-...','856c30ed-...')) as rows_as_user,
  count(*) filter (where matched_user_id in ('887b34cb-...','856c30ed-...')) as rows_as_matched_target
from daily_matches;
-- => total_rows=1600, rows_as_user=0, rows_as_matched_target=0
-- CONFIRMED: neither bot account appears in the live daily_matches table.
-- (full output saved to outputs/matchmaking-investigation.json)

grep -rn "INTO public.daily_matches\|INTO daily_matches\|from('daily_matches')\.insert" --include="*.sql" --include="*.ts" --include="*.py" .
-- => no matches; no code in this repo inserts into daily_matches at all.

